<title>USA: NY Gov to answer Lilco merger questions.</title>
<headline>NY Gov to answer Lilco merger questions.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>New York Gov. George Pataki will hold a Town Hall meeting at 1900 EDT/2300 GMT May 7 on the proposed agreement between the Long Island Power Authority, Long Island Lighting Co and Brooklyn Union Gas Co, the governor's office said Monday.</p>
<p>The meeting at Norwood Avenue School in the Village of Northport in the Town of Huntington is open to the public, which will have an opportunity to ask questions about the agreement, the statement continued.</p>
<p>It quoted Pataki as saying, &quot;I look forward to meeting the people of Long Island to hear their views on this landmark agreement.&quot;</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
